4.1 Decomposition of Unbounded Fan‑In Gates.

The Joshi et al. depth‑3 lower bound applies to QAC⁰ circuits with unbounded fan‑in Toffoli gates. Our circuit avoids this bound by (a) exceeding depth 3, and (b) decomposing large fan‑in gates into cascades of bounded‑fan‑in (3‑input) gates. This decomposition is valid in QAC⁰ because any unbounded gate can be replaced by a tree of bounded gates with logarithmic depth in the fan‑in, preserving constant‑depth overall.

