10.3 Comparison with Pinnacle Architecture (Iceberg Quantum, arXiv:2602.11457).

The Pinnacle Architecture achieves RSA‑2048 factoring with < 100k physical qubits using QLDPC codes and fault‑tolerant logical operations. Our NISQ‑era design requires \approx 840k physical qubits—approximately 8× more—but uses physical‑level gates without logical encoding. Both share the requirement of microsecond code cycles and error rates \sim 10^{-3}. The Pinnacle approach targets logical qubit operations, while ours relies entirely on error mitigation of physical gates. The NISQ advantage is earlier feasibility; the fault‑tolerant advantage is lower qubit count.

